# Gate mod reference (AHG)

When changing Automatic / Hotkey Gates (`auto-gate/`), **check these working B42 Workshop mods first** before inventing new toggle/sync/auto-close logic. Prefer their patterns over novel AHG-only approaches.

## Reference mods (Steam Workshop)

| Workshop ID | Mod | Local path (after steamcmd download) |
|-------------|-----|--------------------------------------|
| `3722192974` | Auto Gate Motor | `F:/Games/steamcmd/steamapps/workshop/content/108600/3722192974/` |
| `3594285774` | HydeCo Automatic Garage Doors + Gates | `F:/Games/steamcmd/steamapps/workshop/content/108600/3594285774/` |
| `3777510303` | Automatic Door Controller / Sensor Gate | `F:/Games/steamcmd/steamapps/workshop/content/108600/3777510303/` |
| `3629503450` | Remote Gate Opener (SP) | `F:/Games/steamcmd/steamapps/workshop/content/108600/3629503450/` |

If a folder is missing: `steamcmd +login anonymous +workshop_download_item 108600 <id> +quit` (steamcmd at `F:/Games/steamcmd/steamcmd.exe`).

## Patterns to copy

- **One `ToggleDoor(player)`** on a **canonical** handle (double-door index 1 when available). Vanilla syncs the rest of the group.
- Always pass a **living IsoPlayer** into `ToggleDoor` (auto-close: borrow nearest online player). Do not call `toggleGroup(..., nil)`.
- Sync locks/modData with `syncIsoObject` / `transmitModData` — **not** `transmitUpdatedSpriteToClients` after a successful `ToggleDoor`.
- Do **not** second-pass every leftover leaf with `ToggleDoorSilent` — that desyncs multi-tile assemblies (HydeCo warning).

## Anti-patterns (do not reintroduce)

```lua
-- BAD: poke every leaf
for _, piece in ipairs(group) do piece:ToggleDoorSilent() end

-- BAD: hard-refuse whole gate because one leaf's getSprite() is nil
if not getSprite(piece) then return "GateCorrupted" end

-- BAD: force sprite transmit after ToggleDoor
piece:transmitUpdatedSpriteToClients()
```

```lua
-- GOOD: GateMotor / HydeCo style
local handle = AHG.getCanonicalGateHandle(group)
handle:ToggleDoor(actor)  -- actor = triggering player or AHG.findActorForToggle(...)
```
